{"model":"qwen2.5-coder:7b","created_at":"2026-11-28T16:59:24.806938Z","response":"### Evidence Classification and Recommendations\n\n#### Evidence Classification:\n1. **iOS Native App Behavior**:\n   - The iOS app uses `UIActivityViewController` for sharing, which does not return a completion flag indicating success or cancellation.\n   - The app handles the dismissal of the share sheet without verifying the destination, which could lead to incomplete backups.\n\n2. **Expo Swift Module**:\n   - The Expo module resolves the promise unconditionally, regardless of the user's action in the share sheet.\n   - This behavior is consistent with the iOS native app, which does not return a completion flag.\n\n3. **React Native Component**:\n   - The React Native component for reminders (`FigmaReminders`) uses a sticky header and bottom navigation, which can be improved for better usability.\n   - The component handles the display of reminders based on their status (upcoming, overdue, completed, memory dates), which is functional but could be improved for better accessibility.\n\n#### Recommendations:\n1. **iOS Native App**:\n   - **Verify Share Sheet Destination**: Ensure that the app verifies the destination before marking the backup as successful. This can be done by checking if the file exists at the destination after the share sheet is dismissed.\n   - **Return Completion Flag**: Modify the `UIActivityViewController` completion handler to return a completion flag indicating success or cancellation.\n\n2. **Expo Swift Module**:\n   - **Conditional Promise Resolution**: Modify the Expo module to resolve the promise only if the user completes the share action, not just dismisses the share sheet.\n\n3. **React Native Component**:\n   - **Improve Accessibility**: Ensure that the sticky header and bottom navigation are accessible and do not interfere with the user's ability to interact with the component.\n   - **Consistent UI**: Ensure that the UI elements are consistent and do not leave the viewport, which can be improved by adjusting the layout and positioning.\n\n### Code Snippets for Recommendations\n\n#### iOS Native App:\n```swift\nactivityController.completionWithItemsHandler = { (activityType, completed, returnedItems, error) in\n    if completed {\n        promise.resolve(nil)\n    } else {\n        promise.reject(\"User cancelled the share action\", \"User cancelled the share action\", nil)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Expo Swift Module:\n```swift\nactivityController.completionWithItemsHandler = { (activityType, completed, returnedItems, error) in\n    if completed {\n        promise.resolve(nil)\n    } else {\n        promise.reject(\"User cancelled the share action\", \"User cancelled the share action\", nil)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### React Native Component:\n```jsx\nconst formatReminderDate = (date, time) =\u003e {\n    const parsed = new Date(`${date}T${time}:00`);\n    if (Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime())) return `${date} · ${time}`;\n    return parsed.toLocaleString(undefined, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric', hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit' });\n};\n\nexport type MemoryDueItem = { id: string; title: string; due: string };\nexport type FigmaRemindersProps = {\n    coverage?: { eligible: number; armed: number; through: Record\u003cstring, number\u003e; available: boolean } | null;\n    showTitles?: boolean;\n    privacyBusy?: boolean;\n    onToggleTitles?: () =\u003e void;\n    onRenewAlerts?: () =\u003e void;\n","done":true,"done_reason":"length","context":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,80328,9464,7388,9489,2530,16546,27480,3395,315,1790,9867,65908,29295,13,8774,2530,3395,1172,13,25094,30774,49465,25,8162,3689,4052,6632,9755,7013,6682,2473,9755,41510,1831,278,26,5702,8145,5181,18975,20527,2393,504,35835,11,714,10275,51323,23670,4688,63297,2041,13451,429,5181,13,3665,7348,47709,15592,220,21,24,24,65,19,20,16,13,16048,9867,906,7